<title>JAPAN: Japan 96/97 copper cable shipments seen up 2.3%.</title>
<headline>Japan 96/97 copper cable shipments seen up 2.3%.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese copper wire and cable shipments are expected to have climbed 2.3 percent in 1996/97 from the previous year, the Japanese Electric Wire and Cable Makers' Association said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The figure was revised up from a March prediction of a 1.9 percent increase.</p>
<p>The association gave the following predictions on Japanese 1996/97 copper wire and cable shipments, compared with the previous year (previous figures in brackets. in tonnes):</p>
<p>			1996/97			change</p>
<p>    Shipments   1,054,172  (1,050,600)     +2.3 pct (+1.9 pct)</p>
<p>    Telecoms	 41,968     (42,000)     +1.0 pct (+1.0 pct)</p>
<p>    Elec Power    125,246    (125,500)     -7.3 pct (-7.1 pct)</p>
<p>    Electrical    278,460    (277,700)     -1.6 pct (-1.8 pct)</p>
<p>    Automobile     71,439     (71,300)    +10.1 pct (+9.9 pct)</p>
<p>    Constr'n	 392,909   (391,000)     +8.9 pct (+8.4 pct)</p>
<p>    Other	    95,246     (95,700)     +6.9 pct (+7.4 pct)</p>
<p>    Exports	  48,904     (47,300)    -13.7 pct (-16.6 pct)</p>
<p>----</p>
<p>    Orders	 1,051,271 (1,051,300)     +1.3 pct (+1.3 pct)</p>
<p>    Foreign orders  50,999    (50,600)    -12.0 pct (-12.8 pct)</p>
